/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 89 0 R
/T (The Student Council Election Tally System is a Java console-based application designed to automate the voting and result calculation process for student council elections. This system efficiently manages candidate information, accepts votes from voters, and automatically computes results to determine the winner. The project demonstrates fundamental Java programming concepts including primitive data types, arrays, control flow statements, and algorithms through a practical real-world application that addresses the inefficiencies of manual voting systems.)
/E (The Student Council Election Tally System is a Java console-based application designed to automate the voting and result calculation process for student council elections. This system efficiently manages candidate information, accepts votes from voters, and automatically computes results to determine the winner. The project demonstrates fundamental Java programming concepts including primitive data types, arrays, control flow statements, and algorithms through a practical real-world application that addresses the inefficiencies of manual voting systems.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
